{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"63e625b40af48ded","name":"card_unit_cameronians","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/CovertOp/units/card_unit_cameronians","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"CAMERONIANS","text":"Draw 2 cards when you give your second order in a turn.","flavorText":"The Cameronians (Scottish Rifles) was a rifle regiment of the British Army which was formed in 1881 and served in the Second Boer War, WWI and later WWII. At the outbreak of WWII, the 1st Battalion was stationed in India, but in 1942 it was deployed in Burma and saw combat in the Burma Campaign as part of the 39th Indian Division. The 2nd Battalion was deployed to France in 1939 as part of the British Expeditionary Force, and after the Dunkirk evacuation in 1940 it participated in the Allied invasion of Sicily and later the Allied invasion of Italy. After serving in the Italian Campaign from 1943 to1944, the battalion participated in the North West Europe Campaign in 1945. The 6th and 7th Battalions were deployed to France as part of the 52nd (Lowland) Infantry Division to provide cover for the Allied withdrawal at Dunkirk, before returning to Britain. After the Normandy Landings in June 1944, the battalions took part in the North West Europe Campaign from 1944 to 1945. The 9th Battalion participated in the Normandy landings in 1944 as part of the 15th (Scottish) Infantry Division and saw action in the North West Europe Campaign from 1944 to 1945. After the war the regiment was reduced to one battalion and would serve in the British Army until it was disbanded in 1968.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":7,"operationCost":1,"attack":7,"defense":8},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_cameronians","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_cameronians_title","SourceString":"CAMERONIANS","LocalizedString":"CAMERONIANS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":7,"defense":8,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":7,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_cameronians_text","SourceString":"Draw 2 cards when you give your second order in a turn.","LocalizedString":"Draw 2 cards when you give your second order in a turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_cameronians_history","SourceString":"The Cameronians (Scottish Rifles) was a rifle regiment of the British Army which was formed in 1881 and served in the Second Boer War, WWI and later WWII. At the outbreak of WWII, the 1st Battalion was stationed in India, but in 1942 it was deployed in Burma and saw combat in the Burma Campaign as part of the 39th Indian Division. The 2nd Battalion was deployed to France in 1939 as part of the British Expeditionary Force, and after the Dunkirk evacuation in 1940 it participated in the Allied invasion of Sicily and later the Allied invasion of Italy. After serving in the Italian Campaign from 1943 to1944, the battalion participated in the North West Europe Campaign in 1945. The 6th and 7th Battalions were deployed to France as part of the 52nd (Lowland) Infantry Division to provide cover for the Allied withdrawal at Dunkirk, before returning to Britain. After the Normandy Landings in June 1944, the battalions took part in the North West Europe Campaign from 1944 to 1945. The 9th Battalion participated in the Normandy landings in 1944 as part of the 15th (Scottish) Infantry Division and saw action in the North West Europe Campaign from 1944 to 1945. After the war the regiment was reduced to one battalion and would serve in the British Army until it was disbanded in 1968.","LocalizedString":"The Cameronians (Scottish Rifles) was a rifle regiment of the British Army which was formed in 1881 and served in the Second Boer War, WWI and later WWII. At the outbreak of WWII, the 1st Battalion was stationed in India, but in 1942 it was deployed in Burma and saw combat in the Burma Campaign as part of the 39th Indian Division. The 2nd Battalion was deployed to France in 1939 as part of the British Expeditionary Force, and after the Dunkirk evacuation in 1940 it participated in the Allied invasion of Sicily and later the Allied invasion of Italy. After serving in the Italian Campaign from 1943 to1944, the battalion participated in the North West Europe Campaign in 1945. The 6th and 7th Battalions were deployed to France as part of the 52nd (Lowland) Infantry Division to provide cover for the Allied withdrawal at Dunkirk, before returning to Britain. After the Normandy Landings in June 1944, the battalions took part in the North West Europe Campaign from 1944 to 1945. The 9th Battalion participated in the Normandy landings in 1944 as part of the 15th (Scottish) Infantry Division and saw action in the North West Europe Campaign from 1944 to 1945. After the war the regiment was reduced to one battalion and would serve in the British Army until it was disbanded in 1968."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Guard","EHelpBubbleTypes::Trigger"],"hasGuard":true,"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/CandidateArtwork/Summer_24/t_cameronians.t_cameronians","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Rebellion","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/CAMERONIANS.CAMERONIANS","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":510.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_cameronians_photo","SourceString":"Men of the 2nd Battalion, Cameronians (Scottish Rifles), in position up in the mountains of Italy, 1943.","LocalizedString":"Men of the 2nd Battalion, Cameronians (Scottish Rifles), in position up in the mountains of Italy, 1943."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryL'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/